WEBVTT

00:07.042 --> 00:09.417
- [groans]
- [guard] Come on!

00:11.708 --> 00:13.916
[Dr. Merati]
"They that love beyond the world

00:13.917 --> 00:15.208
cannot be separated by it.

00:15.542 --> 00:17.583
Death cannot kill what never dies."

00:17.917 --> 00:20.874
[Governor] With Vanessa, at least
I had a sense someone had his ear,

00:20.875 --> 00:22.499
someone could rein him in.

00:22.500 --> 00:24.999
Pressure on my office is immense.
I'm getting it from all sides.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.750
Hi, Marge. I am here to solve
your City Hall problem.

00:29.208 --> 00:31.249
[Buck] We work for a man
who can change your life.

00:31.250 --> 00:34.458
All he asks in return is loyalty.
Make a choice.

00:34.958 --> 00:36.624
- What is this?
- Daniel, please.

00:36.625 --> 00:38.499
I don't even know
if I can protect you anymore.

00:38.500 --> 00:39.707
Protect me from what?

00:39.708 --> 00:41.417
- [cell phone buzzes]
- From him.

00:43.208 --> 00:46.416
[Fisk] We have reason to believe
that Matt Murdock survived the attack.

00:46.417 --> 00:48.499
Help find the lawyer from Hell's Kitchen.

00:48.500 --> 00:50.749
Let's bring this hero home.

00:50.750 --> 00:51.792
Thank you.

00:52.667 --> 00:54.916
- [groans]
- I can't let you do it, Karen.

00:54.917 --> 00:58.457
[Karen] What if this doesn't end
until one of you goes down?

00:58.458 --> 01:00.333
Push those motherfuckers back!

01:02.458 --> 01:03.707
Holy shit.

01:03.708 --> 01:05.875
Karen fuckin' Page.

01:15.208 --> 01:18.917
[sirens wailing in distance]

01:22.583 --> 01:23.583
[man] One avocado.

01:26.167 --> 01:28.291
[reporter 1] According to
city officials, vigilantes...

01:28.292 --> 01:29.666
[reporter 2]
...riots at City Hall...

01:29.667 --> 01:32.708
[reporter 3] Last night's attack
on City Hall by criminals...

01:33.542 --> 01:36.624
- [man yells indistinctly]
- [sirens wail, helicopter hovers]

01:36.625 --> 01:39.167
- [reporter 4] Protesters...
- [reporter 5] ...attacked by Task Force.

01:41.875 --> 01:43.917
- Three injured.
- [reporter 4] Two dead.

01:45.333 --> 01:48.833
[reporter 6] Mayor Fisk vows
to restore order to this city.

01:50.042 --> 01:53.457
[♪ psychedelic rock music playing,
David Bowie "It Ain't Easy"]

01:53.458 --> 01:57.333
♪ When you climb
to the top of the mountain ♪

01:57.458 --> 02:00.667
♪ Look out over the sea ♪

02:01.458 --> 02:07.707
♪ Think about the places, perhaps
where a young man could be ♪

02:07.708 --> 02:12.249
♪ Then you jump back down
to the rooftops ♪

02:12.250 --> 02:15.457
♪ Look out over the town ♪

02:15.458 --> 02:19.124
♪ Think about all of the strange things ♪

02:19.125 --> 02:21.374
♪ Circulating 'round ♪

02:21.375 --> 02:27.292
♪ It ain't easy ♪

02:28.333 --> 02:33.542
♪ It ain't easy to get to heaven
when you're goin' down ♪

02:35.833 --> 02:40.582
♪ Well, all the people
have got their problems ♪

02:40.583 --> 02:42.708
♪ That ain't nothin' new ♪

02:44.125 --> 02:47.832
♪ With the help of the good Lord ♪

02:47.833 --> 02:52.957
♪ We can all pull on through ♪

02:52.958 --> 02:54.582
[inmates chattering indistinctly]

02:54.583 --> 02:58.041
♪ And get there in the end ♪

02:58.042 --> 03:01.457
♪ Sometimes it'll take you right up ♪

03:01.458 --> 03:04.166
♪ And sometimes down again ♪

03:04.167 --> 03:11.124
♪ It ain't easy ♪

03:11.125 --> 03:16.249
♪ It ain't easy to get to heaven
when you're goin' down ♪

03:16.250 --> 03:20.791
- [door buzzes open, closes]
- ♪ It ain't easy ♪

03:20.792 --> 03:23.041
[woman] I don't know.
Come on, everybody.

03:23.042 --> 03:24.707
Hey, where are my cigarettes?

03:24.708 --> 03:29.458
♪ It ain't easy to get to heaven
when you're goin' down ♪

03:49.167 --> 03:50.625
[Fisk] Hello, Miss Page.

03:52.875 --> 03:55.792
You have... taken people from me.

03:58.458 --> 04:00.750
And out there, they believe that you're...

04:01.208 --> 04:02.542
a hero.

04:03.417 --> 04:05.125
Yet I believe in order.

04:06.833 --> 04:08.125
And you are a criminal.

04:08.875 --> 04:09.875
Worse,

04:10.167 --> 04:12.875
you're the sidekick
of a deranged vigilante.

04:14.750 --> 04:15.750
You,

04:16.042 --> 04:18.000
broken and deluded,

04:18.667 --> 04:20.500
you abet his crimes.

04:21.167 --> 04:22.167
For what?

04:23.083 --> 04:24.208
Love?

04:25.458 --> 04:26.792
Ha!

04:45.000 --> 04:47.167
You know,
I've never seen you scared before.

04:49.292 --> 04:50.500
I kinda like it.

04:51.583 --> 04:53.874
No, not fear.

04:53.875 --> 04:55.667
[gasps, winces]

04:56.167 --> 04:57.582
- [choking]
- Order,

04:57.583 --> 04:58.583
Miss Page.

04:59.292 --> 05:00.292
Order.

05:00.542 --> 05:01.874
No, no.

05:01.875 --> 05:04.624
No, you took it too far last night,
and you know it.

05:04.625 --> 05:06.582
And the city knows it!

05:06.583 --> 05:08.875
[choking]

05:09.833 --> 05:12.750
[gasps and coughs]

05:13.708 --> 05:15.542
You have one phone call.

05:16.917 --> 05:18.416
Choose it wisely.

05:18.417 --> 05:20.708
[pants, chuckles softly]

05:26.250 --> 05:29.542
[♪ theme music playing]

07:07.792 --> 07:10.333
[snoring]

07:12.167 --> 07:14.457
- [gasps]
- Good morning, sunshine.

07:14.458 --> 07:15.791
Jessica.

07:15.792 --> 07:17.332
Wait. Hold, hold, hold on.

07:17.333 --> 07:19.082
Listen, before you choose violence--

07:19.083 --> 07:21.041
You sent your assholes to my house.

07:21.042 --> 07:23.541
That was a mistake. They were
just supposed to tell you to back off.

07:23.542 --> 07:24.874
With my daughter there.

07:24.875 --> 07:27.166
I would never hurt your kid--
I love children.

07:27.167 --> 07:28.374
You listen to me.

07:28.375 --> 07:31.624
If you ever come at me
or Danielle ever again,

07:31.625 --> 07:33.375
- I swear to God, I will kill you.
- [groans]

07:33.875 --> 07:35.416
- Do you understand me?
- Yeah.

07:35.417 --> 07:36.500
Please don't kill me.

07:37.458 --> 07:39.957
Also, I'm not really sure you can anymore,

07:39.958 --> 07:43.083
'cause a little birdie said your powers
ain't what they used to be.

07:46.458 --> 07:48.250
Speaking of little birdies,

07:48.917 --> 07:50.249
you're talkin' a lotta shit

07:50.250 --> 07:53.332
for a guy sittin' there in his underwear
with very limited options.

07:53.333 --> 07:56.750
Don't forget, I am the only one
that can connect you

07:57.167 --> 07:58.167
with Luke.

08:02.792 --> 08:04.041
Where is he?

08:04.042 --> 08:06.332
He is overseas.
He's doin' the Lord's work,

08:06.333 --> 08:07.333
so you don't have to.

08:07.792 --> 08:11.291
- You're behind Fisk's arms deal.
- No, I'm not.

08:11.292 --> 08:13.999
Because a couple
anti-social vigilantes blew 'em up.

08:14.000 --> 08:15.999
No arms, no deal. [scoffs]

08:16.000 --> 08:18.582
- Thanks for that, by the way.
- Why are you covering for him?

08:18.583 --> 08:19.667
I'm not, not anymore.

08:20.208 --> 08:21.500
It's actually the opposite.

08:23.208 --> 08:24.792
The Governor wants Fisk...

08:25.417 --> 08:27.166
- out.
- Good, that's...

08:27.167 --> 08:28.291
That's great news.

08:28.292 --> 08:31.291
Yeah, except he just went apeshit
on his own voters.

08:31.292 --> 08:32.708
I don't think she can do it.

08:33.417 --> 08:36.333
The way I see it,
this goes all kinds of wrong

08:36.667 --> 08:38.250
for Governor McCaffrey.

08:39.958 --> 08:43.833
[scoffs] Oh, Christ.

08:44.958 --> 08:46.625
[Matt] Fisk is gonna kill the Governor?

08:47.083 --> 08:48.750
[Jess] That's what Charles suggested.

08:49.042 --> 08:50.374
Very strongly.

08:50.375 --> 08:51.375
And you believe him?

08:52.000 --> 08:54.500
This guy was working with Fisk
until about a minute ago.

08:55.167 --> 08:58.082
I don't believe a word that asshole says,
but in this case...

08:58.083 --> 08:59.750
- Yeah.
- ...it does track.

09:00.833 --> 09:04.583
[sighs] She's the only one
who can revoke the Freeport's charter.

09:05.708 --> 09:08.708
If Fisk puts one of his puppets
in the Governor's office,

09:09.708 --> 09:10.708
New York is his.

09:11.292 --> 09:13.333
And we are on another rooftop.

09:13.667 --> 09:16.499
Yeah, I'm meeting a friend.
Cherry, Jessica. Jessica, Cherry.

09:16.500 --> 09:18.208
Hey, big fan of your work.

09:18.750 --> 09:19.750
Go on.

09:20.208 --> 09:21.208
And?

09:22.375 --> 09:24.707
- Karen's at the 15th Precinct.
- Nice, thank you, Cherry.

09:24.708 --> 09:26.374
All right, now, hold on there, cowboy.

09:26.375 --> 09:27.874
They booked her legit.

09:27.875 --> 09:30.042
Prints, photo, phone call, the works.

09:30.542 --> 09:32.624
They're fast-trackin' her
to Vigilante Court.

09:32.625 --> 09:35.624
You go in there and bust her out,
you are the criminal he says you are.

09:35.625 --> 09:36.957
She's not safe there.

09:36.958 --> 09:39.249
If he was gonna hurt her,
he'd have done it already.

09:39.250 --> 09:42.750
Look, I'm told he went to the precinct,
they talked, he left.

09:44.125 --> 09:45.167
Fisk?

09:45.708 --> 09:46.875
Son of a bitch.

09:48.292 --> 09:49.417
He's making it legal.

09:51.125 --> 09:52.624
We have anybody at the 15th?

09:52.625 --> 09:54.792
We do. Come on, Matt, I'm all over this.

09:56.958 --> 09:59.083
And you? You stickin' around?

10:01.208 --> 10:02.707
I haven't decided yet.

10:02.708 --> 10:03.874
City needs you.

10:03.875 --> 10:06.124
Tsk. I've heard that before.

10:06.125 --> 10:07.542
[chuckles] Me, too.

10:08.292 --> 10:09.958
- Nice to meet you, Cherry.
- You, too.

10:10.583 --> 10:11.583
Matt.

10:13.042 --> 10:15.124
So, what do ya think?
Are you gonna hit the 15th?

10:15.125 --> 10:17.082
I don't know. There might be another way.

10:17.083 --> 10:18.583
- We--
- I can't help you there.

10:19.167 --> 10:20.957
I did what I came here to do.

10:20.958 --> 10:22.625
I got Charles off my ass.

10:23.875 --> 10:25.624
I need to get home. I have Danielle.

10:25.625 --> 10:28.416
I know, you don't need to explain.
I understand.

10:28.417 --> 10:29.833
Fisk isn't gonna stop.

10:31.500 --> 10:33.167
Unless someone puts him down.

10:33.500 --> 10:35.125
Forgotten how encouraging you were.

10:36.500 --> 10:37.708
Don't get yourself killed.

10:40.083 --> 10:41.250
The city needs you.

10:54.083 --> 10:55.875
[bones cracking]

11:12.208 --> 11:13.208
So...

11:15.000 --> 11:16.000
what now?

11:17.417 --> 11:18.875
You wanted one good deed, right?

11:20.125 --> 11:21.667
So we could balance the scales?

11:22.167 --> 11:23.291
- Yeah.
- All right.

11:23.292 --> 11:24.875
- Sure.
- I got it for you.

11:27.208 --> 11:28.583
But first, know this.

11:31.167 --> 11:32.625
I hate you for Foggy.

11:35.125 --> 11:36.582
I hate you for Father Lantom,

11:36.583 --> 11:37.833
for Agent Nadeem.

11:39.625 --> 11:43.083
And every life you've wasted for no reason
other than your own twisted soul.

11:45.458 --> 11:46.917
Part of me wants to kill you.

11:49.625 --> 11:50.625
And...

11:52.417 --> 11:54.083
part of me needs to forgive you.

11:55.458 --> 11:56.458
Yeah.

11:58.708 --> 12:00.375
Well... [clears throat]

12:03.250 --> 12:04.250
Thanks.

12:04.958 --> 12:06.041
Don't do that.

12:06.042 --> 12:07.792
It's not for you, it's for them.

12:08.792 --> 12:10.207
Now go, disappear,

12:10.208 --> 12:11.417
die, I don't care.

12:12.875 --> 12:14.292
But if you mean what you say,

12:15.750 --> 12:18.042
you wanna do one good thing
in a life full of shit,

12:18.667 --> 12:19.750
I got it for ya.

12:21.500 --> 12:24.083
You know I can't make any promises, right?

12:28.083 --> 12:29.542
Wouldn't believe you if you did.

12:37.667 --> 12:39.250
What do you want me to do?

12:40.500 --> 12:42.667
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

12:45.917 --> 12:47.792
[police sirens wailing]

12:52.167 --> 12:53.750
[footsteps approaching]

13:03.083 --> 13:04.083
Brett.

13:05.000 --> 13:06.750
- Hey.
- Hey, Karen.

13:08.042 --> 13:09.124
It's been a while.

13:09.125 --> 13:10.125
Yeah.

13:11.000 --> 13:13.416
[sighs] Wondered why
they brought me to the 15th.

13:13.417 --> 13:16.166
Hey, you know, Chief of Detective
gets to pull a few strings.

13:16.167 --> 13:18.042
Yeah, yeah. Hotshot, huh?

13:21.500 --> 13:22.500
Fisk was here.

13:23.833 --> 13:24.833
I know.

13:25.458 --> 13:26.750
Only so much I can do.

13:27.833 --> 13:28.833
I know.

13:33.083 --> 13:34.417
- What are you doing?
- [unlocking]

13:35.417 --> 13:36.417
Come with me.

13:38.083 --> 13:39.083
Come.

13:43.917 --> 13:45.083
Let's go.

13:56.125 --> 13:57.667
[Daredevil sighs in relief]

14:01.833 --> 14:03.500
- I'm so sorry.
- I'm sorry.

14:03.917 --> 14:05.957
I'm sorry,
I shouldn't have said what I did.

14:05.958 --> 14:06.958
You know...

14:08.083 --> 14:10.375
we all gotta stop meeting up like this.

14:11.167 --> 14:12.792
I can't cover for that long, but...

14:13.458 --> 14:14.624
you got one minute.

14:14.625 --> 14:15.707
- Okay.
- Thank you.

14:15.708 --> 14:16.916
Listen, we don't
have much time,

14:16.917 --> 14:18.417
- I need--
- I can't go with you.

14:18.792 --> 14:20.667
No, I know. I didn't come to get you.

14:21.042 --> 14:22.458
Fucking great minds, huh?

14:24.375 --> 14:27.624
Look, I don't know what this is, but
it feels like an opportunity. I think...

14:27.625 --> 14:29.708
I have to stay.
I have to face him in court.

14:33.250 --> 14:34.792
They tell you he came to see me?

14:35.542 --> 14:37.667
- You okay?
- [sighs] I'm alive.

14:38.875 --> 14:39.917
He's different.

14:41.042 --> 14:42.582
I don't know
what's going on in his mind,

14:42.583 --> 14:45.291
but he's scheming, and he's planning,
and he's way the hell ahead of us.

14:45.292 --> 14:46.707
I just don't think we can run.

14:46.708 --> 14:47.708
Yeah.

14:48.292 --> 14:50.250
'Cause he's losing the city
and he knows it.

14:51.333 --> 14:54.792
So, he's gonna prosecute you
and humiliate you.

14:56.042 --> 14:57.250
Publicly, legitimately,

14:57.958 --> 14:59.542
and make everyone cheer for it.

15:03.917 --> 15:05.208
Can't say it's not smart.

15:08.875 --> 15:10.792
- That means there'll be cameras.
- Mmm-hmm.

15:12.125 --> 15:13.750
- Exactly.
- Holy shit.

15:14.917 --> 15:15.917
Turns out,

15:16.333 --> 15:18.792
we may have to cross lines
to stop him. Just...

15:19.625 --> 15:20.875
not the ones you think.

15:22.708 --> 15:23.708
Well, then...

15:30.000 --> 15:31.333
No. No.

15:32.083 --> 15:33.083
Matt, you can't.

15:34.750 --> 15:35.875
Yes, I can.

15:38.458 --> 15:40.208
[Brett] All right, time's up.
Let's go.

15:54.250 --> 15:56.417
- I'll be there when you need me.
- [sniffles]

15:57.125 --> 15:58.125
Better be.

16:14.708 --> 16:16.249
[Hochberg] Aiding and abetting murder,

16:16.250 --> 16:19.457
providing material support
to known terrorist, Daredevil.

16:19.458 --> 16:22.375
And that's to say
nothing of inciting a riot.

16:22.708 --> 16:24.832
Just a matter of picking
our strongest charges.

16:24.833 --> 16:26.417
Charge her on all of them.

16:26.750 --> 16:28.083
Convict her on all of them.

16:29.042 --> 16:31.625
- Well, sir, given the time crunch--
- All of them.

16:33.375 --> 16:34.375
Right.

16:34.917 --> 16:35.917
Sir.

16:36.417 --> 16:39.250
Do you know the AG
is gonna want to be involved?

16:40.792 --> 16:42.167
Oh, uh...

16:43.750 --> 16:45.666
Well, what he and Albany wants

16:45.667 --> 16:47.333
is irrelevant at this point.

16:48.958 --> 16:49.958
[knocking on door]

16:52.750 --> 16:55.457
- Dr. Glenn.
- Sir, you asked to see me?

16:55.458 --> 16:56.875
[Fisk] Yes, please come in.

16:57.375 --> 16:59.708
Mr. Hochberg and I,
we were finished, weren't we?

17:00.417 --> 17:02.250
Uh... Of course.

17:03.792 --> 17:04.792
Dr. Glenn,

17:05.583 --> 17:06.999
it's always such a pleasure.

17:07.000 --> 17:08.082
I...

17:08.083 --> 17:11.958
might need a little of your expertise
on this trial, if I may.

17:12.792 --> 17:13.792
Of course.

17:18.083 --> 17:21.250
District Attorney Hochberg is
an interesting fellow, isn't he?

17:22.875 --> 17:25.082
He's a very skilled litigator.

17:25.083 --> 17:26.625
He makes my skin crawl.

17:27.125 --> 17:28.125
[chuckles softly]

17:28.750 --> 17:30.250
Lawyers, you know, they...

17:31.500 --> 17:34.417
use words to twist the truth, don't they?

17:36.542 --> 17:38.167
I think I know what you mean.

17:38.458 --> 17:39.542
I imagine you do.

17:41.833 --> 17:43.292
I wanted to check on you...

17:44.625 --> 17:45.917
person-to-person.

17:47.625 --> 17:48.750
How are you, sir?

17:50.333 --> 17:51.750
I... I don't know.

17:53.125 --> 17:54.750
I haven't been asked that.

18:03.250 --> 18:04.292
I always...

18:07.125 --> 18:09.500
accepted love as a prison.

18:13.833 --> 18:16.457
I just never expected

18:16.458 --> 18:18.292
to be in it alone.

18:19.417 --> 18:21.208
[Heather] Condolences are meaningless.

18:21.667 --> 18:23.375
Thoughts and prayers do nothing.

18:24.417 --> 18:27.082
No one tells you the truth
in times like this,

18:27.083 --> 18:28.083
which is...

18:29.042 --> 18:30.208
This is gonna hurt.

18:31.792 --> 18:32.792
And...

18:33.375 --> 18:34.417
we don't know when,

18:35.042 --> 18:36.458
or if it's going to end.

18:38.167 --> 18:39.167
No.

18:40.833 --> 18:41.833
Well, I...

18:42.708 --> 18:43.708
I, uh...

18:45.458 --> 18:47.292
I appreciate your words.

19:03.750 --> 19:06.041
Mayor Fisk, I am so sorry,

19:06.042 --> 19:07.875
- I was--
- You don't have to apologize.

19:08.917 --> 19:10.458
It's curious, isn't it?

19:10.792 --> 19:12.500
When we act on impulse...

19:15.125 --> 19:17.249
we surprise even ourselves.

19:17.250 --> 19:18.792
I'd like to think I have

19:19.375 --> 19:20.916
more self-control than that.

19:20.917 --> 19:22.125
But you didn't.

19:24.125 --> 19:26.958
No. [chuckles softly]

19:32.083 --> 19:34.917
- [♪ suspenseful music playing]
- [sirens wailing]

19:40.500 --> 19:43.667
- [camera shutters clicking]
- [crowd clamoring indistinctly]

19:52.958 --> 19:55.500
[clamoring continues]

20:17.917 --> 20:19.583
- [BB] Can I get my shit back?
- No.

20:21.208 --> 20:23.125
This is kidnapping, you know.

20:24.792 --> 20:26.832
Okay, look, I understand that you're mad,

20:26.833 --> 20:28.541
- but--
- No, I'm not mad.

20:28.542 --> 20:29.832
I'm more than mad.

20:29.833 --> 20:31.458
Mad doesn't even begin to cover it.

20:32.875 --> 20:35.082
I can't keep stalling Buck.

20:35.083 --> 20:36.416
Dude, fuck him!

20:36.417 --> 20:37.708
Fuck him? Fuck you!

20:38.292 --> 20:40.749
Look, I get it, you used me, I used you.

20:40.750 --> 20:43.583
But I'm sorry, I thought
we actually had each other's backs.

20:44.625 --> 20:46.375
Your City Without Fear bullshit?

20:46.875 --> 20:48.082
It fucked us.

20:48.083 --> 20:50.583
So, what, you were working
with Karen Page?

20:55.125 --> 20:56.125
Wow.

20:56.583 --> 20:58.457
- How could you?
- How could I?

20:58.458 --> 21:01.124
I started The BB Report in my dorm room.

21:01.125 --> 21:04.250
I put every dime
and every hour of my life into it.

21:04.625 --> 21:07.208
Okay, people trusted it. It was real.

21:07.583 --> 21:11.707
And you turned it into some plastic
commercial for Fisk's fascist New York.

21:11.708 --> 21:14.416
- I didn't see you complaining.
- Okay. Well, clearly,

21:14.417 --> 21:17.708
you didn't see City Without Fear.
That's complaining.

21:18.458 --> 21:20.832
And all for what?
So that you can get outta Staten

21:20.833 --> 21:22.917
- and get a douchebag condo?
- Stop!

21:24.208 --> 21:25.541
He killed my uncle.

21:25.542 --> 21:26.833
- You don't know that.
- Yes,

21:27.458 --> 21:29.417
I do. And you do, too.

21:30.125 --> 21:32.874
You've just decided to turn a blind eye,
and that is your problem.

21:32.875 --> 21:34.041
Fine.

21:34.042 --> 21:35.625
Whatever. I did.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.291
It is, but you don't understand.

21:38.292 --> 21:39.792
That doesn't matter anymore.

21:40.250 --> 21:44.708
Because right now, Buck Cashman
is waiting for me to hand you over to him.

21:45.833 --> 21:47.042
And if I don't,

21:47.667 --> 21:48.875
then he comes after me.

21:50.000 --> 21:51.083
And then you,

21:51.583 --> 21:52.583
and my mom,

21:53.250 --> 21:54.750
and anyone I care about.

21:55.125 --> 21:58.208
So, BB, you should be fucking terrified
right now, 'cause I am.

21:58.875 --> 21:59.875
Then...

22:00.458 --> 22:02.125
we should probably get out of here.

22:03.083 --> 22:04.458
Yeah, we probably should.

22:07.333 --> 22:09.082
- Give me my phone.
- No.

22:09.083 --> 22:11.417
- Why?
- Because I don't trust you.

22:12.625 --> 22:14.374
Just give me a second to fucking think.

22:14.375 --> 22:16.250
Just sit there and let me think.

22:16.750 --> 22:18.792
[scoffs] Okay.

22:22.625 --> 22:23.707
We need a safe house.

22:23.708 --> 22:25.499
What are you, Jason Bourne?

22:25.500 --> 22:26.583
No, just...

22:28.042 --> 22:30.417
Some place Buck doesn't know about.

22:34.125 --> 22:36.207
I have a friend. A finance buddy.

22:36.208 --> 22:38.167
Works mostly in Hong Kong. I'll text him.

22:38.625 --> 22:39.792
Great.

22:41.750 --> 22:42.750
[sighs]

22:46.458 --> 22:47.749
[vibrates]

22:47.750 --> 22:50.291
[reporter] ...Assistant District Attorney
Kirsten McDuffie...

22:50.292 --> 22:52.792
Daniel is proving to be
quite a team player.

22:53.375 --> 22:54.375
Yes, he is.

22:54.792 --> 22:57.292
It's not easy to make the hard decisions.

22:58.750 --> 23:00.708
You think Karen Page knows?

23:01.042 --> 23:02.208
[Buck] Knows what, sir?

23:02.667 --> 23:04.792
That she is the wounded soldier

23:05.292 --> 23:07.167
screaming in the field,

23:07.583 --> 23:10.500
drawing her comrades
into the line of fire.

23:14.375 --> 23:16.833
- [people chattering indistinctly]
- [woman] Really?

23:17.208 --> 23:18.667
- That's good.
- Either way...

23:33.042 --> 23:34.500
[court officer] All rise.

23:42.333 --> 23:44.207
[Chief Justice Waters]
District Attorney Hochberg,

23:44.208 --> 23:45.750
your opening statement.

23:48.958 --> 23:49.958
Your Honors...

23:53.125 --> 23:56.375
I stand before you today
to ask that you convict

23:57.625 --> 23:59.292
and that you punish this woman,

24:00.083 --> 24:02.583
this criminal, Karen Page,

24:03.333 --> 24:06.332
for the crime she has committed
against our great city.

24:06.333 --> 24:08.875
Your Honors, I could argue
my client's innocence.

24:09.625 --> 24:12.750
I could argue
the illegitimacy of this court.

24:13.708 --> 24:15.583
I could argue against

24:16.000 --> 24:17.416
the Safer Streets Act.

24:17.417 --> 24:21.417
But first, I want you to think on
one very important concept.

24:23.000 --> 24:24.417
What is a vigilante?

24:25.333 --> 24:28.166
Is it he or she who breaks the law

24:28.167 --> 24:32.125
in order to get
their own version of justice? Or...

24:32.500 --> 24:34.666
is a vigilante the last resort

24:34.667 --> 24:36.249
to obtain the justice

24:36.250 --> 24:38.999
that a broken society
can no longer supply?

24:39.000 --> 24:41.333
The evidence will show that

24:42.042 --> 24:44.000
Miss Page is not a hero.

24:45.000 --> 24:46.666
She's not a "freedom fighter"

24:46.667 --> 24:48.791
for a noble resistance. No.

24:48.792 --> 24:49.792
No, she's...

24:50.292 --> 24:51.375
a criminal

24:52.167 --> 24:55.625
responsible for the destruction
of innocent human lives.

24:56.167 --> 24:59.374
[Kirsten] Your Honors,
you have a duty to this city,

24:59.375 --> 25:02.458
and you have a duty
to the ideals of this court,

25:04.125 --> 25:08.332
and fulfilling that duty
can only come to one conclusion.

25:08.333 --> 25:09.416
Guilty.

25:09.417 --> 25:10.583
Not guilty.

25:12.833 --> 25:13.833
Thank you.

25:14.667 --> 25:16.791
Prosecution can now call
its first witness.

25:16.792 --> 25:18.750
Your Honors, before we proceed...

25:19.625 --> 25:21.416
I'd like to bring in my co-counsel.

25:21.417 --> 25:23.332
[Hochberg] What-- Co-counsel?

25:23.333 --> 25:25.375
What, already calling for backup?

25:29.125 --> 25:30.792
[audience gasps]

25:31.208 --> 25:33.250
Matthew Murdock
for the defense, Your Honors.

25:34.042 --> 25:35.957
- [woman 1] Oh, my God!
- [man] Is that Matt Murdock?

25:35.958 --> 25:38.291
- [woman 2] Matt Murdock?
- [woman 3] My God. It's Matt Murdock?

25:38.292 --> 25:39.916
[Chief Justice Waters] Order in the court.

25:39.917 --> 25:41.707
[reporter] In a shocking turn of events,

25:41.708 --> 25:44.374
Matthew Murdock,
the missing lawyer from Hell's Kitchen,

25:44.375 --> 25:46.457
has just walked into the courtroom.

25:46.458 --> 25:49.041
Despite a citywide search,
Murdock has not been seen

25:49.042 --> 25:51.999
since the destruction of
his Brooklyn apartment months ago.

25:52.000 --> 25:55.291
Murdock is well known for
his heroic act of saving Mayor Fisk

25:55.292 --> 25:56.874
from vigilante gunfire.

25:56.875 --> 25:59.458
But he has now reappeared,
apparently, to support...

26:05.167 --> 26:06.374
[Matt] Officer Powell,

26:06.375 --> 26:10.166
tell me, what is the mission statement
for the Anti-Vigilante Task Force?

26:10.167 --> 26:13.791
To interdict, apprehend,
and prosecute extra-legal vigilantes

26:13.792 --> 26:15.541
to the fullest extent of the law.

26:15.542 --> 26:17.207
"To the fullest extent of the law"?

26:17.208 --> 26:18.708
That sounds serious.

26:19.292 --> 26:20.375
As a heart attack.

26:21.542 --> 26:22.832
[Matt] Huh.

26:22.833 --> 26:25.667
And, Officer Powell,
who formed the Task Force, and...

26:26.417 --> 26:28.875
created these, uh, parameters?

26:30.292 --> 26:31.292
Mayor Fisk.

26:33.292 --> 26:34.374
Of course.

26:34.375 --> 26:36.583
[Kirsten] Can you tell me about
those scars on your face?

26:37.083 --> 26:40.582
I got these in a firefight
with Daredevil and Frank Castle.

26:40.583 --> 26:42.792
- In Mr. Murdock's apartment?
- Yes.

26:44.583 --> 26:46.041
[Kirsten] Why were you there?

26:46.042 --> 26:49.833
Um, we were performing a welfare check.

26:51.292 --> 26:52.458
Welfare check?

26:54.458 --> 26:57.250
With assault rifles
and MRAP personnel carriers?

26:57.958 --> 27:00.791
I don't know, seems like
a lot of hardware for a blind lawyer.

27:00.792 --> 27:02.458
[audience chuckles]

27:05.083 --> 27:06.375
Was the defendant there?

27:09.375 --> 27:11.458
I was told she drove the getaway vehicle.

27:13.000 --> 27:14.417
You were told?

27:15.125 --> 27:17.250
What else did Officer Powell
tell you to do?

27:18.458 --> 27:20.167
Did he tell you to kill Hector Ayala?

27:20.833 --> 27:22.791
- Or maybe that was Mayor Fisk.
- Objection.

27:22.792 --> 27:25.166
Immaterial, misleading, and prejudicial.

27:25.167 --> 27:27.082
Sustained. Ms. McDuffie,

27:27.083 --> 27:29.249
I will caution you against these theatrics

27:29.250 --> 27:31.749
and remind you that
there's no jury to play to here.

27:31.750 --> 27:33.208
Sure about that, Your Honor?

27:36.750 --> 27:37.832
No further questions.

27:37.833 --> 27:38.833
Thank you.

27:46.917 --> 27:49.707
- [line rings]
- [woman on phone] Alan Steverud's office.

27:49.708 --> 27:50.750
It's me.

27:51.000 --> 27:52.292
I need the Attorney General.

27:53.625 --> 27:55.000
- [AG Steverud] Steverud.
- Alan,

27:55.375 --> 27:58.167
I think it's time we move forward
on the suspension paperwork.

27:58.667 --> 28:01.750
Fisk's reign is over.
But we do need to move quick, though.

28:03.083 --> 28:05.250
No, it's-- It's gotten outta hand. It's...

28:06.292 --> 28:08.125
Yeah-- Our window is now.

28:10.042 --> 28:11.042
Okay.

28:32.042 --> 28:33.042
Daniel?

28:34.292 --> 28:35.292
What's going on?

28:37.375 --> 28:38.375
Daniel!

28:40.208 --> 28:42.708
You know, it's not just Fisk and Buck.

28:43.542 --> 28:44.542
It's me, too.

28:45.458 --> 28:46.583
I've done things.

28:47.125 --> 28:49.500
Really, really fucked up things.

28:51.000 --> 28:52.375
What're you talking about?

28:54.625 --> 28:56.167
I went upstate with Buck,

28:57.500 --> 28:59.583
to the Catskills, and we buried a body.

29:01.208 --> 29:02.208
Jesus.

29:06.208 --> 29:08.167
And I wish I didn't know I did that.

29:13.875 --> 29:14.875
But I can't...

29:15.708 --> 29:17.833
have anyone else knowing I did that.

29:38.167 --> 29:39.167
Come on.

29:47.000 --> 29:48.583
This isn't a safe house, is it?

29:49.167 --> 29:50.749
Daniel. Daniel!

29:50.750 --> 29:52.125
Daniel, please! Daniel!

29:53.667 --> 29:57.500
Is this really the person you wanna be?
[breathing heavily]

30:07.000 --> 30:08.291
Fuck! Fuck.

30:08.292 --> 30:10.625
Come on. Come on, before he sees.

30:14.625 --> 30:16.083
Here, take this

30:16.583 --> 30:19.332
and go. Don't go home.
Don't tell me where.

30:19.333 --> 30:21.417
And do not go anyplace
he would look, okay?

30:22.167 --> 30:24.875
- What're you gonna do?
- Doing the right thing. Just let me.

30:27.917 --> 30:28.917
Thank you.

30:29.917 --> 30:31.083
Of course.

30:33.542 --> 30:34.708
Just make it count.

30:45.125 --> 30:47.667
[Chief Justice Waters] This court
is adjourned until tomorrow morning.

30:51.625 --> 30:52.875
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

30:54.583 --> 30:56.333
I've got it. You focus on the rest.

30:57.750 --> 31:00.457
- That went as well as I thought.
- Yeah, I know. It's okay.

31:00.458 --> 31:01.458
It's okay.

31:02.208 --> 31:03.291
Be careful.

31:03.292 --> 31:04.292
[Matt] You, too.

31:09.792 --> 31:11.167
They're not leaving, are they?

31:13.125 --> 31:14.292
No, they're not.

31:15.500 --> 31:17.000
[Cole] Cameras are all off, sir.

31:20.625 --> 31:22.792
[♪ sinister music playing]

31:31.917 --> 31:32.917
Hold here.

31:39.125 --> 31:40.125
Come on!

31:45.750 --> 31:48.458
[guns clicking, engine revving]

31:49.333 --> 31:50.874
Run! Cherry!

31:50.875 --> 31:52.083
Look out!

31:53.125 --> 31:54.167
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

31:59.417 --> 32:00.667
Get down!

32:06.875 --> 32:08.083
- Holy shit!
- Fuck!

32:10.750 --> 32:12.167
Take the wheel! Take the wheel!

32:16.083 --> 32:17.750
Now! Get her outta here!

32:18.958 --> 32:20.042
[Kirsten] Matt!

32:23.375 --> 32:24.792
[groans]

32:30.375 --> 32:31.833
[winces]

32:35.167 --> 32:36.208
[grunts]

32:45.583 --> 32:46.958
[♪ ominous music playing]

32:56.083 --> 32:57.167
[gasps]

32:57.542 --> 32:58.750
[choking]

33:01.708 --> 33:03.042
[groans]

33:09.958 --> 33:11.417
[strains]

33:12.417 --> 33:14.292
[groans]

33:14.708 --> 33:17.375
- [body thuds]
- [breathes heavily]

33:29.375 --> 33:31.917
[groans]

33:33.208 --> 33:34.833
[sirens wailing]

33:43.833 --> 33:45.042
[door closes]

33:51.208 --> 33:52.208
Hey.

33:58.167 --> 33:59.208
Where is she?

34:03.000 --> 34:04.083
She's not coming.

34:25.500 --> 34:26.708
Where is she, Daniel?

34:28.042 --> 34:30.125
I think she had a birthday party.

34:30.750 --> 34:32.167
[sighs]

34:33.958 --> 34:35.042
[scoffs]

34:37.667 --> 34:38.875
[sighs]

34:40.042 --> 34:41.083
[rips]

34:44.292 --> 34:45.667
Now, sooner or later...

34:49.375 --> 34:50.625
we both know...

34:53.875 --> 34:55.000
you're gonna tell me.

34:59.792 --> 35:01.333
Fuck you, Buck.

35:04.083 --> 35:05.125
[sighs]

35:06.208 --> 35:07.875
[both grunting]

35:13.125 --> 35:14.417
Fuck!

35:18.750 --> 35:20.957
[Daniel coughing]

35:20.958 --> 35:23.625
[Daniel groaning]

35:25.500 --> 35:27.750
[Daniel] No! No!

35:30.625 --> 35:33.083
[door buzzes open]

35:38.042 --> 35:39.083
Miss Page,

35:40.083 --> 35:41.667
it's nice to finally meet you.

35:43.750 --> 35:44.750
Ms. Glenn.

35:46.833 --> 35:48.207
Are you here for Fisk?

35:48.208 --> 35:49.875
I'm part of the Mayor's office, yes.

35:50.875 --> 35:54.666
I also conduct psychological evaluations
for the District Attorney's office.

35:54.667 --> 35:55.833
[scoffs]

35:57.042 --> 35:58.042
I'll pass.

36:00.083 --> 36:01.583
Doesn't really work that way.

36:02.917 --> 36:05.792
I'm gonna ask a series of
true or false questions.

36:06.167 --> 36:07.167
Please...

36:07.958 --> 36:09.207
answer truthfully.

36:09.208 --> 36:10.582
There are no wrong answers.

36:10.583 --> 36:11.792
True or false?

36:12.833 --> 36:14.583
"I like mechanics magazines."

36:15.792 --> 36:19.583
You know, the Minnesota Multiphasic
Personality Inventory is out of date.

36:20.375 --> 36:21.874
- I can game it.
- Mmm.

36:21.875 --> 36:22.875
Most people can.

36:24.292 --> 36:26.125
Maybe we should try something else.

36:27.250 --> 36:28.458
What did you have in mind?

36:32.875 --> 36:34.208
I'm in love with this man.

36:36.792 --> 36:38.667
He's completely inaccessible. He's...

36:39.417 --> 36:40.708
distant, complicated.

36:42.125 --> 36:43.292
There are nights where I...

36:44.125 --> 36:47.792
I fall asleep in bed next to him,
totally unsure of who he is.

36:50.583 --> 36:51.583
Worries me.

36:52.833 --> 36:53.917
As it should.

36:55.333 --> 36:56.750
It's also totally hot.

36:58.042 --> 36:59.666
I'm sure you can understand.

36:59.667 --> 37:00.667
So,

37:01.125 --> 37:03.542
- what does that say about me?
- [clears throat]

37:04.500 --> 37:05.582
[beeps]

37:05.583 --> 37:07.000
That's a very good question.

37:08.250 --> 37:09.250
I mean,

37:09.958 --> 37:12.458
what kind of person
kills their own brother?

37:13.875 --> 37:16.042
The Mayor's office has detailed files.

37:16.958 --> 37:20.417
Fratricide is very rare.

37:22.292 --> 37:24.375
- Was Kevin molesting you?
- Don't.

37:26.000 --> 37:27.000
No.

37:28.000 --> 37:29.374
No, it wasn't like that.

37:29.375 --> 37:30.541
[Heather] I'm sure.

37:30.542 --> 37:32.750
[chuckles] Did you feel powerful

37:33.375 --> 37:35.083
when you murdered James Wesley?

37:36.375 --> 37:37.958
After a lifetime of, I don't know,

37:38.500 --> 37:40.500
being used as a puppet by all these men.

37:41.292 --> 37:42.292
Daddy,

37:42.625 --> 37:43.625
brother,

37:43.875 --> 37:46.500
- Frank Castle.
- Fuck you!

37:47.125 --> 37:49.500
[chuckles] Funny.

37:50.333 --> 37:51.833
That's where the nerve is.

37:55.000 --> 37:56.000
Does Matt know?

37:57.542 --> 37:59.583
- You wanna know what I think?
- Mmm.

38:01.500 --> 38:04.499
I know that Matt, that mystery beside me,
loves me in a way

38:04.500 --> 38:05.999
that makes every contradiction,

38:06.000 --> 38:08.167
every conflict in him
and in me a part of us.

38:09.000 --> 38:11.792
And I'm willing to bet that that's
the part that you can't really understand.

38:13.542 --> 38:16.332
Professionals call that transference.

38:16.333 --> 38:17.792
Yeah, well, I call it the truth.

38:21.042 --> 38:23.291
You were friends
with Vanessa Fisk, weren't you?

38:23.292 --> 38:27.291
I'm not answering any personal questions.
That's unprofessional.

38:27.292 --> 38:30.667
She had my friend Foggy killed.
You know that? Is that in those files?

38:31.917 --> 38:33.124
Jesus.

38:33.125 --> 38:34.749
Matt really hurt you, didn't he?

38:34.750 --> 38:36.667
Enough that you'd run to them
to feel safe.

38:37.375 --> 38:38.499
Please.

38:38.500 --> 38:40.083
Look, I get it. I'm so sorry.

38:40.375 --> 38:42.041
[groans]

38:42.042 --> 38:43.333
[yells in pain]

38:45.667 --> 38:48.333
- [groans]
- Don't pity me.

38:48.875 --> 38:51.625
[chuckling] Too late.

38:52.625 --> 38:56.958
[groans, laughs]

38:57.250 --> 38:58.250
Is that all you got?

38:59.333 --> 39:00.416
Not even close.

39:00.417 --> 39:01.917
[chuckles]

39:05.083 --> 39:07.542
- We should do this some other time.
- I can't wait.

39:11.375 --> 39:13.250
- [groans]
- [Buck] Where, Daniel?

39:14.458 --> 39:15.750
I don't enjoy this.

39:18.542 --> 39:20.583
I don't know where she is.

39:27.292 --> 39:28.875
- [gun clicks]
- [Daniel] Oh, fuck!

39:31.708 --> 39:33.167
This isn't Helmand, Buck.

39:33.667 --> 39:34.875
[gun cocks]

39:35.417 --> 39:36.792
Last chance.

39:43.708 --> 39:45.292
[Matt groaning]

39:46.833 --> 39:48.667
[breathing raggedly]

39:50.625 --> 39:52.708
[panting]

39:56.333 --> 39:57.542
[grunts]

39:57.792 --> 39:59.999
[pants]

40:00.000 --> 40:02.583
[Daniel] What is followin' his orders
gonna do for you?

40:04.083 --> 40:06.083
How long till you're on the floor

40:06.542 --> 40:08.292
with a gun pointed at your head?

40:12.083 --> 40:14.250
- [groans]
- [Matt] Saint Jude...

40:16.625 --> 40:19.833
patron of difficult cases...
[chuckles dryly]

40:22.500 --> 40:24.375
of things almost despaired of...

40:26.750 --> 40:27.750
pray for me.

40:30.375 --> 40:32.167
I am so helpless and alone.

40:33.958 --> 40:36.708
Please pray for me that God come to me
in my hour of need,

40:38.833 --> 40:41.708
and I receive consolation

40:42.500 --> 40:44.458
in all my tribulations and sufferings.

40:53.083 --> 40:54.083
And that...

40:54.958 --> 40:56.292
I may bless God...

40:59.542 --> 41:01.292
- with the elect for all eternity.
- [groans]

41:02.375 --> 41:04.500
[breath trembling]

41:07.917 --> 41:09.000
Amen.

41:12.708 --> 41:14.083
[sighs]

41:14.875 --> 41:17.500
[panting]

41:46.542 --> 41:49.542
[door opens and closes]
